{title: The Hill of Samaria}
{subtitle: 1 Kings 16:15–16; 16:21–22; 16:23–24; 16:25–26; 16:28–29}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 77}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Dm] |
| [Dm] | [Bb] | ×4

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
The [Dm]troops were encamped against Gibbet[Bb]hon
They [Dm]heard that Zimri had struck down the [Bb]king
All [Gm]Israel in the camp that very [Bb]day
[Dm]Proclaimed the commander Omri their new [Bb]king
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
He [Dm]bought the hill of Samaria from She[Bb]mer
Built up the [Dm]city with two talents of sil[Bb]ver
He named it [Gm]after the owner of the [Bb]ground
A [C]capital that would not be un[Dm]bound [Bb]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
The [Dm]people were split into two distinct [Bb]sides
Half [Dm]followed Tibni son of Ginath to [Bb]reign
Half [Gm]followed Omri in the battle lines [Bb]
But [Dm]Omri proved stronger than Tibni a[Bb]gain
[Dm]Tibni died and the war [Bb]was done
Omri became [Dm]king in the thir-ty-first year of A[Bb]sa
[Gm]He reigned twelve years in the northern [Bb]land
[C]Six years in Tirzah before he could [Dm]rest
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
He bought the hill of Samaria from She[Bb]mer
Built up the [Dm]city with two talents of sil[Bb]ver
He named it [Gm]after the owner of the [Bb]ground
A [C]capital that would not be un[Dm]bound
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Bb]He did evil in [Dm]the eyes of the Lord
[Bb]Acting more wickedly than all before [Dm]him
He [Bb]followed the sin of Jeroboam [Dm]son of Nebat
[Bb]Provoking the God of Israel to [C]anger
With worthless idols that brought them [Dm]shame
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Bb]Omri rested with his fa[Dm]thers
[Bb]Buried in [Dm]Samaria
[Bb]His son Ahab took the [Dm]throne
Con[C]tinuing the ways of the [Dm]old
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
He bought the hill of Samaria from She[Bb]mer
Built up the [Dm]city with two talents of sil[Bb]ver
He named it [Gm7]after the owner of the [Bb]ground
A [C]capital that would not be un[Dm]bound
{end_of_chorus}

